 "verdict": "Not worth running daily in this form. On the same inputs the API ranks person-launch pairs clearly worse than a 6-feature logistic baseline (AUC 0.60 vs 0.74), names fewer backers (recall at N 18.8% vs 25.7%), orders a backer's own picks worse (0.60 vs 0.67), and its raw P is uncalibrated (mean 0.43 vs a 3% base rate; Brier 0.229 vs 0.029). Averaging its rank with the baseline lowers AUC (0.71). Cheap ($0.68 per 1,000 person-days), so a re-test with a different framing is affordable, but not as a daily line.",
 "notes": [
  "Population is E5's re-read rule (complete, held before D, re-read after D closed) with a 50/50 backer/active-non-backer sample: recall at N here is not comparable 1:1 to E5's ~29% on all held people.",
  "REPORT.md could not be written by this agent (the harness refused a .md report file); the pre-registration is preregistration.json (committed before scoring, commit 1465c16e) and the report is in this file and the commit message."
 ]
